/// else in the path builder is traced from the Mac binary (BIN labels at the code sites).
/// </summary>
public static class PathApproximations
{
	public static readonly IReadOnlyList<(string Id, string Rule)> Entries = new[]
	{
		("PATH-017", "PATH-PAUSE-WINDOW: the ordinary-WM pump (bounded admission then drain: topmost eligible receiver, stable screen/element lifetime, separate movement capture, saved release owner) is implemented; the pause key P (tp.exe 0x40bf70 → 0x409350(1)) toggles a window (the global handle 0x7cb2cc, 0x4a27f0 → 0x47ed80; the offline focus-loss pause 0x4092a0(1) → 0x4a2790 builds it too): a full-screen layer (0x65dd7b(1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0x7ff, 0x5ff), flags 1, the 'lolight' backdrop) appended as the last child of the root, under the panel 5094 (174,500)-(1874,900) of table 0x752e00. The hit test 0x65db25 takes a shown window with flag bit 1 and lets the last such child win (0x65dd7b appends a new window after its siblings), so the layer is the hit window of every point and, with the focus (0x65e59b), of every key over the windows that existed when it was built; its procedure 0x4a2680 uses only the P key and the panel's animation (0x65e72d, table 0x752ed0) and hands the rest to the default procedure 0x65f6d1, which forwards nothing, so the park click handler 0x4879d0 (called only from the HUD window's procedure, 0x488768) and the camera's input 0x42a760 (called only by the procedures of the HUD, the hidden-HUD overlay and the chat mode) get no message under it; the click route and the camera follow that here, and OpenTPW's speed pause (the HUD's speed buttons, the numpad, a park loaded paused) builds no layer, as 0x409350 is the only builder besides the focus loss. Round 11 N: the P window is drawn (the full-canvas 'lolight' model over the windows that existed when it was made, then the paused banner of table 0x752e00, 1700 x 400 at (174,500), animating by table 0x752ed0 every 35 ms: 0x47ed80, 0x4a2680) and, as it holds the focus and is the hit window of every point, no key, text or wheel reaches the screens below it. Not ported: the alternate buffered-input mode (its selector and pump are not read), and the stored pick of the click dispatcher. Read: the click dispatcher 0x4879d0 (14 cases over the hover kind 0x7c24f4, called from the HUD window's procedure 0x488768 right after the classifier 0x486d90, 0x48875f) takes no message coordinates; it acts on the stored pick word 0x7b05cc, which the world frame 0x54e2b0 rewrites every frame by ray-picking from the pointer (0x45bf90 -> 0x45d560: the cell z * 128 + x + 1, or 0) and skips while 0x790ab0 & 0x16 (the ride and walk eye cameras, bits 0x04 and 0x02); its meaning depends on the hover kind 0x7c24f4 (4 a cell, 3 and 6 records of the park at +0x294, 5 records at +0x6cde). A click therefore acts on the previous world frame's pick under the pointer, where OpenTPW picks under the pointer when the click arrives; the dispatcher's 14 cases are the open part (evidence needed: the alternate buffered-input mode's pump and the dispatcher's cases)"),
